※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4380 LANG_AUXV_NOT_AN_INTEGER
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4211 LANG_CALL_WRONG_ARGUMENT_COUNT

※ What the auxiliary vector is asked about is the number the kernel gives a
※ type of entry, and nothing else is one: a truth value, a character or a
※ floating-point number is refused (4380), as is asking about no type or about
※ two at once (4211).  A whole number of any width and either signedness is
※ accepted, widened by its own signedness.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let page: u64 = ⎕auxv(true) ?? 0u64
    let size: f64 = 6f64
    let more: u64 = ⎕auxv(size) ?? 0u64
    let letter: u64 = ⎕auxv('a') ?? 0u64
    let none: u64 = ⎕auxv() ?? 0u64
    let two: u64 = ⎕auxv(6u64, 33u64) ?? 0u64
    if page + more + letter + none + two = 0u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
